From aa395ca7eafd469b3ba265fdd81ecd649f8b08c6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 02:40:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Rung 4: the founder's whole score shrinks once its neighbour
 is below half its usual size

The difference term alone let crowding pay: on the log size scale a
founder that doubles itself gains about what it loses for halving its
neighbour, so the rung-2 re-fits (a shrub beside the shrub re-fit ends at
21 cells against 367) beat shipped on rung 4 and selection from them moved
nothing. hold_score is now multiplied by min(1, kept / 0.5), kept being
the neighbour's end shoot against its size beside the control -- still
graded, a quarter of its size halves the score.

Measured with `plantrain mode=rungs rungs=hold` (12 layouts, beside every
role), floored hold score, shipped -> rung-2 re-fit -> rung-4 champion from
shipped: tree 2.07 -> 1.94 -> 2.09, shrub 2.76 -> 3.00 -> 3.37, herb
3.57 -> 3.36 -> 3.58, creeper 2.23 -> 2.13 -> 2.27. The re-fits fall to or
below shipped except the shrub; the tree's rung-4 random champion (which
took a herb from 7 flowerings in 8 to 3) drops to 1.43. Shipped beds under
the floor: 3-8 of 48 per role, the noise the floor adds to the control.
`plantrain mode=rungs` now prints the floored hold score per arm.

